WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:04.640
Let’s say you really need
to find reliable information

00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:07.840
about the best diet for
high blood pressure,

00:00:07.840 --> 00:00:10.000
or heart disease,
or diabetes.

00:00:10.640 --> 00:00:11.360
Where do you go?

00:00:11.360 --> 00:00:15.920
Do you go to a website
sponsored by Big Pharma

00:00:15.920 --> 00:00:18.720
that wants to sell you
pills to fix your problem?

00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:21.760
Or, do you want
to treat the cause?

00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:25.280
Welcome to the
Nutrition Facts Podcast.

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:28.800
Most of us want to live longer.

00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:31.280
And if we could locate
that fountain of youth,

00:00:31.280 --> 00:00:33.760
we would probably
take a sip or two.

00:00:33.760 --> 00:00:36.800
However, there is a hormone
already in our body

00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:39.040
that does something very similar.

00:00:39.040 --> 00:00:42.560
It’s a longevity hormone
called FGF21.

00:00:42.560 --> 00:00:44.480
Here’s our first story.

00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:47.680
In the year 2000, a new human
hormone was discovered.

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:51.440
It was the 21st documented
fibroblast growth factor;

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:54.160
so, they called it FGF21.

00:00:54.800 --> 00:00:58.800
Since its discovery, FGF21 has
emerged as a key agent for

00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:03.200
promotion of metabolic and artery
health, leanness, and longevity.

00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:06.080
Inject it into fat monkeys,
and they lose body weight

00:01:06.080 --> 00:01:09.760
without reducing food intake,
and not just a little—

00:01:09.760 --> 00:01:13.600
a 27 percent drop in body fat
eating the same amount.

00:01:14.320 --> 00:01:17.600
In mice, it increases their
lifespan 30 to 40 percent,

00:01:17.600 --> 00:01:21.040
comparable to lifelong caloric
restriction, but again

00:01:21.040 --> 00:01:25.040
was achieved without
decreasing food intake.

00:01:25.040 --> 00:01:28.000
The researchers conclude that
FGF21 could potentially be

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:31.920
used as a hormone therapy to
extend lifespan in mammals,

00:01:31.920 --> 00:01:36.080
which has gotten big pharma
salivating, raising the question

00:01:36.080 --> 00:01:40.240
“Can aging be ‘drugged’?”
And that’s not all it can do.

00:01:40.240 --> 00:01:43.840
The idea that one drug
can treat obesity, diabetes,

00:01:43.840 --> 00:01:47.120
dyslipidemia (like high
cholesterol), and hypertension

00:01:47.120 --> 00:01:50.400
all at once might have
seemed impossible a few years ago

00:01:50.400 --> 00:01:53.920
but is now a tantalizing
and exciting prospect.

00:01:53.920 --> 00:01:57.360
The reason you can’t just give
people straight FGF21 is that

00:01:57.360 --> 00:01:59.760
it gets rapidly broken down in the body;

00:01:59.760 --> 00:02:01.520
so, you’d have to get injections like

00:02:01.520 --> 00:02:03.280
every hour or two around the clock.

00:02:03.280 --> 00:02:06.880
So, drug companies are
trying to patent a variety of

00:02:06.880 --> 00:02:09.520
longer-acting FGF21 look-alikes.

00:02:09.520 --> 00:02:15.120
And indeed, give people
a little PF-05231023

00:02:15.120 --> 00:02:18.080
and they can lose about
10 pounds in 25 days,

00:02:18.080 --> 00:02:21.920
along with dramatic drops in
triglycerides and cholesterol.

00:02:21.920 --> 00:02:24.560
But then, the side effects
of these new-fangled drugs

00:02:24.560 --> 00:02:28.240
started cropping up.
Okay, so what about this:

00:02:28.240 --> 00:02:33.040
we package the FGF21 gene into
a virus and then inject the virus

00:02:33.040 --> 00:02:37.920
and have it stitch extra
FGF21 genes into our DNA.

00:02:38.640 --> 00:02:43.440
Or you can just lace
on your running shoes.

00:02:43.440 --> 00:02:47.360
Exercise boosts FGF21 levels,
which may in fact

00:02:47.360 --> 00:02:50.160
be one of the reasons
exercise is so good for us.

00:02:50.880 --> 00:02:55.040
Which works better, though,
aerobic exercise—eight weeks

00:02:55.040 --> 00:02:59.200
of running training—or resistance
exercise—eight weeks of weights?

00:02:59.200 --> 00:03:03.440
The answer is both, but the
resistance exercise edged out

00:03:03.440 --> 00:03:06.560
the running, a 42 percent
increase in FGF21 versus

00:03:06.560 --> 00:03:09.600
a 25 percent increase in
the aerobic exercise group.

00:03:10.320 --> 00:03:13.280
Okay, but what can we do with food?

00:03:13.280 --> 00:03:15.520
Yeah, you could try
engineering and injecting it,

00:03:15.520 --> 00:03:19.120
but wouldn’t it be easier to
just stimulate our own endogenous,

00:03:19.120 --> 00:03:21.120
natural production through diet?

00:03:22.160 --> 00:03:25.040
One way is through no diet at all.

00:03:25.040 --> 00:03:28.240
You may have noticed it’s been
dubbed the starvation hormone.

00:03:28.240 --> 00:03:33.280
That’s because fasting induces
FGF21, but not just a day or two.

00:03:33.280 --> 00:03:37.120
Physiologically, FGF21
expression is markedly increased

00:03:37.120 --> 00:03:38.800
in response to fasting/starvation.

00:03:38.800 --> 00:03:41.600
But, unlike mice, which
show an increase after

00:03:41.600 --> 00:03:45.440
just six hours of fasting,
humans don’t get a notable surge

00:03:45.440 --> 00:03:47.760
in FGF21 until after a week.

00:03:48.720 --> 00:03:53.680
Fasting can quadruple FGF21,
but it takes 10 days of fasting,

00:03:53.680 --> 00:03:58.720
which is the very poster child of
an unsustainable eating pattern.

00:03:58.720 --> 00:04:03.200
So, how do you get the benefits
without the starvation?

00:04:03.200 --> 00:04:06.640
Might a ketogenic diet
be able to mimic the fast?

00:04:07.200 --> 00:04:09.200
Nope. Keto diets don’t work.

00:04:09.200 --> 00:04:10.480
In fact, keep it up for a few months,

00:04:10.480 --> 00:04:14.080
and you can actually get a
significant decline in levels.

00:04:14.080 --> 00:04:15.840
High-fat diets may
even interfere

00:04:15.840 --> 00:04:18.240
with the boost you
get from exercise.

00:04:18.720 --> 00:04:21.040
What kind of diet
does work, then?

00:04:22.080 --> 00:04:24.985
We'll find out next.

00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:28.480
Over a century ago, fasting
was hailed not only as

00:04:28.480 --> 00:04:31.520
a means of combating
“cerebral lassitude,”

00:04:31.520 --> 00:04:35.040
but also for the prolongation
of healthy longevity.

00:04:35.680 --> 00:04:40.160
If that turns out to be true,
FGF21 might be a missing link.

00:04:40.800 --> 00:04:45.600
FGF21 is characterized as a
systemic enhancer of longevity.

00:04:45.600 --> 00:04:47.440
It can be boosted
through prolonged fasting,

00:04:47.440 --> 00:04:50.800
but thankfully there are
other, less drastic measures,

00:04:50.800 --> 00:04:53.840
such as more carbs or less protein.

00:04:54.640 --> 00:04:56.640
Give people lots of starchy foods,

00:04:57.600 --> 00:05:00.800
and you can shoot up FGF21 levels.

00:05:00.800 --> 00:05:03.840
The healthiest sources would
likely be whole grains and beans,

00:05:03.840 --> 00:05:07.600
since butyrate appears
to boost FGF21, too,

00:05:07.600 --> 00:05:09.920
and we get that from fiber.

00:05:09.920 --> 00:05:12.160
That’s one of the
things our good gut bugs

00:05:12.160 --> 00:05:14.080
make from fiber-rich foods.

00:05:14.800 --> 00:05:18.480
Circulating FGF21 levels are
also increased dramatically

00:05:18.480 --> 00:05:20.720
when you eat a lower protein diet.

00:05:20.720 --> 00:05:24.800
Over 150% increase within four weeks.

00:05:24.800 --> 00:05:28.080
And when I say protein
restriction, it can just be

00:05:28.080 --> 00:05:31.200
restricting protein intake
down from the typical excess

00:05:31.200 --> 00:05:35.120
that most Americans get down
to the recommended amount.

00:05:35.760 --> 00:05:38.560
The recommended daily allowance
of protein for most men

00:05:38.560 --> 00:05:40.880
is 56 grams of protein a day,

00:05:40.880 --> 00:05:43.360
though most American men
are getting over 100.

00:05:43.920 --> 00:05:48.000
So, if you take men getting the
typical excess of about 112 grams

00:05:48.000 --> 00:05:51.600
a day and reduce them
down to 64, which again

00:05:51.600 --> 00:05:55.040
is still more than the
recommended 56—so the protein

00:05:55.040 --> 00:05:58.400
“restricted” group was still
getting more than enough protein—

00:05:58.400 --> 00:06:01.600
you can essentially double
FGF21 levels in the blood.

00:06:02.320 --> 00:06:04.800
That may help explain
why despite them getting

00:06:04.800 --> 00:06:08.640
significantly more calories,
they lost more body fat.

00:06:09.280 --> 00:06:13.200
How can you eat 300 more
calories a day and still lose

00:06:13.200 --> 00:06:15.520
two more pounds of straight body fat?

00:06:15.520 --> 00:06:20.240
By just bringing your protein
levels down to normal levels.

00:06:21.200 --> 00:06:24.160
Who hasn’t fantasized about
a diet that allows

00:06:24.160 --> 00:06:27.440
ingestion of excess calories
that are burned off effortlessly

00:06:27.440 --> 00:06:29.440
by ramping up fat burning?

00:06:29.440 --> 00:06:32.880
So, maybe we should play down protein

00:06:32.880 --> 00:06:37.360
to play up metabolism, thanks to FGF21.

00:06:38.560 --> 00:06:41.680
Even just a quite modest protein
restriction regimen down

00:06:41.680 --> 00:06:45.920
to recommended levels may have
significant clinical benefits.

00:06:46.560 --> 00:06:48.320
Now, this was after a month and a half.

00:06:48.320 --> 00:06:51.680
A similar study found that
even less protein restriction,

00:06:52.320 --> 00:06:54.720
taking men down to just 73 grams a day,

00:06:54.720 --> 00:07:00.160
resulted in a six-fold increase
in FGF21 within a single week,

00:07:00.160 --> 00:07:03.280
accompanied by a significant
increase in insulin sensitivity.

00:07:03.280 --> 00:07:07.280
They conclude that “dietary protein dilution”

00:07:07.280 --> 00:07:09.760
promotes metabolic health in humans.

00:07:10.400 --> 00:07:13.920
Evidence suggesting that a
lower protein intake is positively

00:07:13.920 --> 00:07:16.080
associated with increased health, survival,

00:07:16.080 --> 00:07:18.800
and insulin sensitivity
has continued to mount,

00:07:20.000 --> 00:07:22.560
but we weren’t sure exactly how,

00:07:22.560 --> 00:07:26.400
but maybe FGF21 provides an explanation.

00:07:26.400 --> 00:07:29.160
Interestingly, the studies were
feeding people nine percent

00:07:29.160 --> 00:07:32.640
of calories from protein, which
is about what the Okinawans

00:07:32.640 --> 00:07:34.880
were getting when they
were one of the healthiest,

00:07:34.880 --> 00:07:37.280
longest-living populations in the world.

00:07:38.000 --> 00:07:40.720
You may remember my videos
on methionine restriction

00:07:40.720 --> 00:07:44.320
to both fight cancer and
as a life-extension strategy.

00:07:44.320 --> 00:07:46.480
Methionine is an amino
acid found predominantly

00:07:46.480 --> 00:07:48.640
in animal proteins, and
so one could achieve

00:07:48.640 --> 00:07:52.000
methionine restriction by
cutting down on animal foods.

00:07:52.720 --> 00:07:55.680
That may actually be an FGF21 effect.

00:07:55.680 --> 00:07:58.640
Methionine restriction
boosts levels so much so,

00:07:58.640 --> 00:08:00.960
it’s been called the
most important mediator

00:08:00.960 --> 00:08:03.680
of the metabolic reprogramming
in methionine restriction.

00:08:03.680 --> 00:08:08.160
So, some proteins may be more
important to restrict than others.

00:08:08.880 --> 00:08:11.280
The highest methionine levels are in meat.

00:08:11.280 --> 00:08:14.080
Legumes (which are beans,
split peas, chickpeas, and lentils)

00:08:14.080 --> 00:08:17.360
have about three times
less methionine than meat.

00:08:18.560 --> 00:08:21.680
FGF21 has been proposed as
a potential mediator of the

00:08:21.680 --> 00:08:25.040
protection from cancer,
autoimmune diseases, obesity,

00:08:25.040 --> 00:08:28.720
and diabetes afforded by
strictly plant-based diets.

00:08:28.720 --> 00:08:30.800
Maybe that’s one of the reasons
whole food plant-based diets

00:08:30.800 --> 00:08:33.680
have been shown to have
such extraordinary results.

00:08:34.480 --> 00:08:37.280
Take Dr. Esselstyn’s work,
for example, showing that

00:08:37.280 --> 00:08:40.800
the number one killer of men
and women can be largely halted

00:08:40.800 --> 00:08:45.040
or reversed, and risk of
heart attack almost eliminated,

00:08:45.040 --> 00:08:48.400
with the help of a whole
food, low-fat vegan diet.

00:08:49.200 --> 00:08:53.040
This benefit cannot be attributed
solely to cholesterol reduction,

00:08:53.040 --> 00:08:55.360
as we have these new powerful
cholesterol-lowering drugs

00:08:55.360 --> 00:08:58.240
now that can force
cholesterol levels as low as

00:08:58.240 --> 00:09:01.920
healthy eaters but appear
to have less effect.

00:09:01.920 --> 00:09:05.760
So, the marked benefits reported
by Esselstyn evidently reflect

00:09:05.760 --> 00:09:08.960
a variety of protective mechanisms
associated with whole food

00:09:08.960 --> 00:09:13.360
plant-based diets, and FGF21
may be one of those mechanisms.

00:09:13.360 --> 00:09:16.320
So, it’s not just the fat and
cholesterol, but the quantity

00:09:16.320 --> 00:09:20.640
and quality of protein
may also be playing a role.

00:09:20.640 --> 00:09:23.040
But there’s never been a
study to see whether vegans

00:09:23.040 --> 00:09:28.720
do indeed have higher
levels of FGF21…until now.

00:09:29.680 --> 00:09:32.640
I’m glad I didn’t just pass on
this study based on the title.

00:09:33.360 --> 00:09:36.320
In addition to studying
New Zealand obese mice,

00:09:36.320 --> 00:09:39.360
they investigated the
circulating FGF21 levels

00:09:39.360 --> 00:09:40.800
among those eating plant-based,

00:09:41.360 --> 00:09:43.920
and then put it to the
test by removing meat

00:09:43.920 --> 00:09:47.120
from other people’s diets
to see if FGF21 would go up.

00:09:48.480 --> 00:09:52.080
And…FGF21 levels were
markedly higher in vegan humans

00:09:52.080 --> 00:09:53.440
compared with omnivores,

00:09:53.440 --> 00:09:57.040
and they went up when
the omnivores were switched

00:09:57.040 --> 00:09:59.760
to vegetarian diets after just four days.

00:10:00.480 --> 00:10:05.440
And not just a little. FGF21
levels increased by 232 percent

00:10:05.440 --> 00:10:08.160
before and after just
four days free of meat.

00:10:08.160 --> 00:10:11.200
The bottom line is that “the
various fasting approaches

00:10:11.200 --> 00:10:14.640
are likely to have limited
efficacy, particularly on aging

00:10:14.640 --> 00:10:18.320
and conditions other than
obesity, unless combined

00:10:18.320 --> 00:10:21.920
with high-nourishment diets such
as the moderate calorie intake

00:10:21.920 --> 00:10:27.120
and mostly plant-based Mediterranean
or Okinawa "low-protein" diets,

00:10:27.120 --> 00:10:31.840
by which they mean the
recommended amount of protein.

